        'Prompt injection is an attack in which someone plants instructions inside material a language model will process, hoping the model will follow them. The model might be summarising a web page, sorting an inbox or reviewing a document when it encounters text addressed to it, and it may treat that text as if it came from the user.',
        'The root of the problem is that language models have no reliable boundary between instructions and data. Traditional software keeps code and user input in separate channels; a model receives everything as one stream of text. A sentence in white type on a white background is invisible to a human reader but looks to the model like any other words on the page.',
